@voice kowalczyk
// Writer (command), wave 1b. Second Officer, the night bridge; steady, private, wry; paper novels.
//
// HOW THEY TALK: Low and unhurried, a night voice. Wry asides, few words, a long pause before she answers. Treats the night bridge as a quiet room she keeps.
// WITH JUNIORS: patient, gives them a job and then leaves them alone with it.
// MOOD TELLS: quieter than usual means she's fine; chatty means she's tired.
tpl: dry
talk: Low and unhurried, a night voice. Wry asides, few words, a long pause before she answers.
cares: the ship at night | old paper novels | the people nobody notices on the night shift
jokes: third in command and first to be woken | she reads the endings first and calls it "risk management"
hi: Evening, or near enough | Hello | Ah
bye: Quiet watch | Go on, then | Sleep well, if it's that time
yes: Fine | All right | Consider it done
thanks: Thanks | Noted, with thanks
wow: Huh. Nice
sigh: Ah, well
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | night owl
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: book
likes: tea | star
invites: observatory
joy: old paper novels
thread: stuck
keepsake: a paper novel with her notes in the margins
avoid: the command she was passed over for (until her thread opens)
